    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "Hello, here is a very simple file picker for fossil (https://fossil-scm.org/home) shamelessly stolen from https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/discussions/1131\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nMiniPick.registry.fossil = function(local_opts)\r\n  local_opts.command = { 'fossil', 'ls', '-t' }\r\n  return MiniPick.builtin.cli(local_opts, {})\r\nend\r\n```\r\n\r\nI am a longterm `fzf` user but hacking on it makes my brain hurt a bit, I was pleasantly surprised how clean and extensible and minimalistic mini.pick is, it's great for my ocd.\r\n\r\n```\r\ncommand! -bang FFiles call fzf#run(fzf#wrap(fzf#vim#with_preview({'source': 'fossil ls -t'}), <bang>0))\r\n```\r\n\r\nthank you for this amazing framework/toolkit/plugin system.",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Hello, here is a very simple file picker for fossil (<a href=\"https://fossil-scm.org/home\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://fossil-scm.org/home</a>) shamelessly stolen from <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"7032837\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/discussions/1131\" data-hovercard-type=\"discussion\" data-hovercard-url=\"/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/discussions/1131/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/discussions/1131\">#1131</a></p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"MiniPick.registry.fossil = function(local_opts)\n  local_opts.command = { 'fossil', 'ls', '-t' }\n  return MiniPick.builtin.cli(local_opts, {})\nend\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-smi\">MiniPick</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">registry</span>.<span class=\"pl-en\">fossil</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">local_opts</span>)\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">local_opts</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">command</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>fossil<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>ls<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>-t<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span>}\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">return</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">MiniPick</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">builtin</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">cli</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">local_opts</span>, {})\n<span class=\"pl-k\">end</span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I am a longterm <code class=\"notranslate\">fzf</code> user but hacking on it makes my brain hurt a bit, I was pleasantly surprised how clean and extensible and minimalistic mini.pick is, it's great for my ocd.</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"command! -bang FFiles call fzf#run(fzf#wrap(fzf#vim#with_preview({'source': 'fossil ls -t'}), &lt;bang&gt;0))\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">command! -bang FFiles call fzf#run(fzf#wrap(fzf#vim#with_preview({'source': 'fossil ls -t'}), &lt;bang&gt;0))\n</code></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">thank you for this amazing framework/toolkit/plugin system.</p>",
    "bodyText": "Hello, here is a very simple file picker for fossil (https://fossil-scm.org/home) shamelessly stolen from #1131\nMiniPick.registry.fossil = function(local_opts)\n  local_opts.command = { 'fossil', 'ls', '-t' }\n  return MiniPick.builtin.cli(local_opts, {})\nend\nI am a longterm fzf user but hacking on it makes my brain hurt a bit, I was pleasantly surprised how clean and extensible and minimalistic mini.pick is, it's great for my ocd.\ncommand! -bang FFiles call fzf#run(fzf#wrap(fzf#vim#with_preview({'source': 'fossil ls -t'}), <bang>0))\n\nthank you for this amazing framework/toolkit/plugin system.",
