            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> thank you for this amazing framework/toolkit/plugin system.\r\n\r\nThank *you* for sharing this!\r\n\r\n~~Although you do link to #1131, I'd recommend to provide fully working, copy-pasteable implementation of a picker. So it would need a `wt_switch` definition.~~\r\n\r\nAlso, it is a personal preference, but I'd not put `cwd` in a picker's name. It is usually obvious when calling picker; if not - it is available in info view after `<S-Tab>`.",
            "bodyHTML": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">thank you for this amazing framework/toolkit/plugin system.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Thank <em>you</em> for sharing this!</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><del>Although you do link to <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"7032837\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/discussions/1131\" data-hovercard-type=\"discussion\" data-hovercard-url=\"/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/discussions/1131/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/discussions/1131\">#1131</a>, I'd recommend to provide fully working, copy-pasteable implementation of a picker. So it would need a <code class=\"notranslate\">wt_switch</code> definition.</del></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Also, it is a personal preference, but I'd not put <code class=\"notranslate\">cwd</code> in a picker's name. It is usually obvious when calling picker; if not - it is available in info view after <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;S-Tab&gt;</code>.</p>",
            "bodyText": "thank you for this amazing framework/toolkit/plugin system.\n\nThank you for sharing this!\nAlthough you do link to #1131, I'd recommend to provide fully working, copy-pasteable implementation of a picker. So it would need a wt_switch definition.\nAlso, it is a personal preference, but I'd not put cwd in a picker's name. It is usually obvious when calling picker; if not - it is available in info view after <S-Tab>.",
