                    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
                    "body": "> Although you do link to https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/discussions/1131, I'd recommend to provide fully working, copy-pasteable implementation of a picker. So it would need a wt_switch definition.\r\n\r\ntbh that was my intention and i missed the `wt_switch` part 😅 \r\nhowever when i tested it, it worked...\r\n\r\nI am not advocating for `fossil`'s inclusion, it's pretty niche, i was just wondering if `tool` could be generalized to \"any executable that gives back a list of items\", but `MiniPick.builtin.cli()` seems to do the job.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Although you do link to <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"7032837\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/discussions/1131\" data-hovercard-type=\"discussion\" data-hovercard-url=\"/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/discussions/1131/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/discussions/1131\">#1131</a>, I'd recommend to provide fully working, copy-pasteable implementation of a picker. So it would need a wt_switch definition.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">tbh that was my intention and i missed the <code class=\"notranslate\">wt_switch</code> part 😅<br>\nhowever when i tested it, it worked...</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I am not advocating for <code class=\"notranslate\">fossil</code>'s inclusion, it's pretty niche, i was just wondering if <code class=\"notranslate\">tool</code> could be generalized to \"any executable that gives back a list of items\", but <code class=\"notranslate\">MiniPick.builtin.cli()</code> seems to do the job.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "Although you do link to #1131, I'd recommend to provide fully working, copy-pasteable implementation of a picker. So it would need a wt_switch definition.\n\ntbh that was my intention and i missed the wt_switch part 😅\nhowever when i tested it, it worked...\nI am not advocating for fossil's inclusion, it's pretty niche, i was just wondering if tool could be generalized to \"any executable that gives back a list of items\", but MiniPick.builtin.cli() seems to do the job.",
